{
  "dom_id": "step-q356985",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $u=4$ and $v=-9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $u+v?$",
  "worked_solution": "The value of $u+v$ is the number located a distance $|v|$ from $u$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $v$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $v$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $u=4$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $v=-9$, so the distance we move is $|v|=9.$\n\n- Because $v$ is *negative*, we move $9$ units to the *left* from $4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152428/assets/79c5200c6f0089f7b6cf6be0eec8b97de3ff3a3daa270bfa6e7ae0c480b134f5.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n4+(-9)=-5.\n$$",
